p.src:
To make the variables interact, add a term that cannot be split into an $x$-part and a $y$-part. A simple example is $L
=
\frac{\dot x^2}{2}
+\frac{\dot y^2}{2}
-V(x)-W(y)+\kappa xy.$ Now varying $x$ produces a term proportional to $y$, while varying $y$ produces a term proportional to $x$. The same mixed term governs both directions of influence.

