+O\!\left(\frac{\dot x^4}{c^4}\right).$ 代入[eq:sr5-particle-coupling-c]得到 $\begin{aligned}L_{\mathrm p}
&=
-mc^2-g\phi
+\frac{m\dot x^2}{2}
+\frac{g\phi\,\dot x^2}{2c^2}
+O(c^{-4})\\
&\longrightarrow
\frac{m\dot x^2}{2}-g\phi(x,t),
\end{aligned}$ 其中已略去常数$-mc^2$以及被$c^{-2}$压低的项。结果就是通常的形式$T-V$，因此 $V_{\mathrm p}(x,t)=g\phi(x,t).$

p.src:
To expose the source with minimal algebra, place the particle at rest at the origin. The factor $d\tau$ then equals $dt$, and the interaction part of [eq:sr5-particle-coupling] becomes $S_{\mathrm{int}}
=
-g\int dt\,\phi(\mathbf{0},t).$ This is an integral only along the worldline, whereas [eq:sr5-free-field-action] is an integral over all spacetime. To combine them into one spacetime integral, we need a function that selects the particle’s position.

